instr:
Can't generate styled Markdown PDFs in our report exporter

Our report exporter uses `jspdf-md-renderer` to turn Markdown into PDFs. I need headings, lists, blockquotes, rules and images to work together across pages, with the documented margins and optional security checks for remote images.

```ts
import { jsPDF } from 'jspdf';
import { MdTextRender } from 'jspdf-md-renderer';
const doc = new jsPDF({ unit: 'mm', format: 'a4' });
await MdTextRender(doc, '# Release notes\n\n> Check the rollout.', {
  font: { regular: { name: 'helvetica', style: 'normal' } }, blockquote: { backgroundColor: '#EDF2F7' },
});
```

This should draw the heading and styled quote into the document. Instead, rendering reaches an unfinished body that throws `Error("not implemented")`.

The unfinished pieces are in these files under `src/`:

- `renderer/components/blockquote.ts`, `renderer/components/hr.ts` and `renderer/components/listItem.ts`.
- `security/security-policy.ts` and `store/renderStore.ts`.
- `utils/content-stream.ts`, `utils/handlePageBreak.ts`, `utils/image-utils.ts` and `utils/options-validation.ts`.

